# MRK WooCommerce API Integration Plan

The goal is to fetch MRK metal prices and display them as a new card on the "Tools" page (`src/pages/Reports.tsx`), while keeping the existing metal prices on the Dashboard untouched.

## Proposed Changes

### 1. Create a `MrkPricesCard.tsx` component
Create a new component (`src/components/MrkPricesCard.tsx`) to fetch and display the prices.
- It will fetch data directly from `https://www.mrk.co.za/wp-json/wc/store/v1/products?per_page=100`.
- It will parse the JSON response, filtering or searching for specific products (e.g., "1 OZ Gold Krugerrand", "1 OZ Silver Krugerrand"). 
- Extract the prices (dividing by 100 since WooCommerce stores price in cents) and format them as Rands (ZAR).
- Display a small table or list mimicking the clean UI of the existing dashboard.

> [!NOTE]
> If direct frontend fetching fails due to CORS policies on the MRK server, we will pivot to creating a new Supabase Edge Function (`get-mrk-prices`) to act as a proxy.

### 2. Update `Tools` Page (`src/pages/Reports.tsx`)
- Import and render the `MrkPricesCard` alongside the existing tools grid.
- We will likely place the card above or next to the productivity tools grid so it's clearly visible.

